<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n42820" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ξ.</span></b> 
		
			Pass.
		, pf.
		<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">εἴρῡμαι,</span>
		plpf.
		3pl.
		<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b>
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">εἰρύατο [ῡ</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Il.
					14.30
				</span></i>
			, al., <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ῠ</span>
			<i><span class="en">
				4.248
			</span></i>], <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">εἴρυντο</span> (v. infr.):
				aor.
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐρύσθην</span> or <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">εἰρ-,</span>
			<i><span class="en">
				Hp.
				<u>Epid.</u>
				5.47
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				<u>Mul.</u>
				1.36
			</span></i>:—<i>to be drawn ashore, drawn up in line,</i> of
			ships, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">εἴρυντο νέες ταχὺν ἀμφ᾽ Ἀχιλῆα</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Il.
					18.69
				</span></i>
			 ; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">εἰρύατο νῆες θῖν᾽ ἔφ᾽ ἁλὸς πολιῆς</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					14.30
				</span></i>
			, cf.<i><span class="en">
				4.248
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b>
			<i>to be drawn, attracted,</i> of moisture, Hp.l.c.; <i>to be
				contracted,</i>
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐς τοὔπισθεν ἐρυσθείς,</span> of
			tetanic convulsions, <i><span class="en">
				Id.
				<u>Epid.</u>
				5.47
			</span></i> ; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τὴν γνάθον ἐρυσθεῖσα</span> ib.<i><span class="en">
				4.36
			</span></i>. (<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ϝερῠ-, ϝρῡ-,</span> cf.
				<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ῥῡ-τήρ</span> (<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">βρύτηρ</span>), <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ῥῦ-μα,
			ῥῡ-μός.</span>)</div>
